  "protocol": "Same working binary, one fresh server per condition and budget, native Metal, one slot. Serial execution. Warm 15 -> 8 then 4000 -> 8. Each timing is the median of three uncached 4000 -> 64 streamed requests with greedy decoding, ignore_eos and seed 42. TTFT and request time use client SSE timestamps, TPS=63/(last-first token time). Residency, prefill and DFlash2 selection follow the default profile in both arms. The 24 GiB pair uses 38 layers during decode. Timed runs do not contain diagnostic counters or logit dumps.",
  "correctness": "All emitted token IDs compared with the previously qualified reference at the same cap and mode. At 8 and 12 GiB separate diagnostic builds record actual Metal dispatches and all post-prefill output logits, including rejected draft rows, on matched input IDs, positions and batch widths. Process and managed peak include startup and warmup.",
